This happened to me ONCE and I have yet to be lucky enough to 
repeat the trick...

When starting Nethack, always be a Wizard (not THE Wizard, just the class).
This will get you two rings...
If they just happen to be Poly and Poly Control, wear them and walk
around until the Poly occurs....
Select 'Red Dragon' (or any dragon for that matter)
# Sit down a few times.  You should lay an egg for each time you sit down.
	If not, eat a ration (not the eggs) or such...
Get the eggs, remove the rings.
Kill a shopkeeper if you can IN DRAGON FORM of course!
The poly should wear out before the egg hatch in your backpack.
Of course, since you laid them, the baby dragon think your its mommy/daddy,
and voila - Instant Army of dragons.

I definately recommend only getting 4 dragons.   I once had 5 baby red
dragons, 6 baby garter snakes, and 4 or 5 baby cave spiders.  Great for
nuking opponents, but it slowed the game up so much, and trying to take them
all down stairs was a pain.


